### draft-ietf-v6ops-rfc7084bis: Basic Requirements for IPv6 Customer Edge Routers
* **Presentation**: [7084bis](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-v6ops-7084bis-00)
* **Presenter**: Tim Winters
* **Discussion**:
  * **Draft Updates (-08)**: Updated ULA terminology, referenced RFC 8504bis, updated DHCPv6 references to RFC 9915, clarified DNS proxy language (L22), and added requirements G8/W7 (IPv6 DNS resolution support, RFC 9715 R5/R6 fragmentation recommendations).
  * **M/O Flags**: Combined WAA12 into WAA6 to prevent CEs from dropping DHCP clients/prefixes when M/O flags flap on the WAN interface.
  * **ULAs**: Upgraded ULA generation and advertisement to SHOULD to ensure local in-home connectivity remains functional even when the WAN interface is down.
  * **DNS over TCP & Proxy Concerns**:
    * Ted Lemon raised concerns regarding DNS proxy requirements vs. full-service resolvers (ensuring full-service resolvers are not discouraged) and strongly advocated for enforcing DNS over TCP (referencing RFC 5625 and DNSOP discussions regarding post-quantum cryptography).
    * David Lamparter noted in chat that RFC 5625 already requires DNS over TCP.
    * XiPeng Xiao suggested adding RFC 9715 R7 (fallback to TCP when UDP fails) as a SHOULD/MUST requirement. Tim Winters agreed to review adding R7 and reinforcing DNS over TCP.
  * **ULAs & SNAC**: Lorenzo Colitti and Ted Lemon discussed ULA stability and interaction with SNAC routers, concluding that local CE ULA generation provides helpful stability.

