### draft-ietf-v6ops-icmpext-xlat-v6only-source: Using Dummy IPv4 Address and Node Identification Extensions for IP/ICMP translators (XLATs)
* **Presentation**: [Using Dummy IPv4 Address and Node Identification Extensions for IP/ICMP translators (XLATs)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-v6ops-using-dummy-ipv4-address-and-node-identification-extensions-for-ipicmp-translators-xlats-00)
* **Presenter**: Jen Linkova
* **Discussion**:
  * The document was returned from AD evaluation to address a scoping issue: RFC 6791 assumed stateless translators possessed public IPv4 address pools, which CLATs/translators in v6-only networks lack.
  * **Draft Updates (-03)**: Instead of deprecating RFC 6791, draft-03 updates it: if a public IPv4 address is available, use it; otherwise, use the designated dummy IPv4 address.
  * **Coordination**: Overlapping translation algorithm text is being moved into [draft-ietf-v6ops-rfc7915-bis](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-v6ops-rfc7915-bis/) (presented by Jordi Palet Martinez). The remaining text in `draft-ietf-v6ops-icmpext-xlat-v6only-source` will focus on updating RFC 6791.
  * Tom Hill and Ted Lemon supported progressing the document.

